WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.533
Week 29: Relative Clauses and Unknown Referents. define a requirement identify known and unknown people or things connect complex information

2
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:32.145
Read for the situation. La organización busca a una persona que conozca la región y pueda trabajar de inmediato. Ya entrevistó a un candidato que vivió allí durante cinco años. The organization is looking for a person who knows the region and can work immediately. It has already interviewed a candidate who lived there for five years.

3
00:00:32.145 --> 00:00:41.035
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:41.035 --> 00:00:46.960
Reading activities. Reading activity 69; Reading activity 70

5
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:55.146
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:55.146 --> 00:01:26.780
Model language. La organización busca a alguien que conozca la región. — The organization is looking for someone who knows the region. Necesita a alguien que pueda comenzar de inmediato. — It needs someone who can start immediately. Ya entrevistó a un candidato ideal. — It has already interviewed an ideal candidate. Ese candidato vivió allí cinco años. — That candidate lived there for five years. Sigue buscando más opciones. — It keeps looking for more options.

7
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:36.785
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
